      "title": "Certificate Expiration on Legacy Cache Service (Pre-Migration Flow)",
      "content_summary": "Troubleshooting account lockouts caused by unrotated certificates on the legacy Cache Service.",
      "content_body": "When users report 'account locked out' errors alongside a 'certificate expired warning', verify that the service certificate has been manually rotated. This issue typically occurs because credential rotation is not automatically propagated in the current environment. Check for operator error in the previous renewal logs, as manual steps were often skipped. To resolve, execute the legacy credential rotation script and confirm access review is completed for affected users. Educate customers on the need for manual renewal until the new automated flow is fully deployed."
